   "source": [
    "# Care Operations Analytics - Analysis Walkthrough"\\n\n",
    "### For Hiring Manager Review"\\n\n",
    "This notebook walks through the key analytical findings from the Care Operations Analytics project. All data is synthetic and fictional."\\n\n",
    "**Synthetic Data Statement**: All data in this notebook is entirely synthetic and fictional. No real personal, healthcare, client, employee, or company data is used."\\n\n",
    "**Prerequisites**: Run `python -m src.pipeline` and `python -m src.risk_model` before executing this notebook."\\n\n",
    "---"\\n\n",
    "## 1. Business Problem"\\n\n",
    "A fictional Canadian care-services provider delivers in-home services funded by multiple funders. Leadership needs visibility into:\\n\\n- Funding utilization and possible budget overruns\\n- Claims likely to be rejected or need manual review\\n- Operational problems such as late documentation and worker-capacity constraints\\n- Aging reconciliation exceptions\\n\\n---"\\n\n",
    "## 2. Data and Data-Quality Note"\\n\\n\\n",
    "### Data Sources"\\n\\n\\n",
    "- **clients.csv**: 300 clients across 25 Canadian cities\\n- **workers.csv**: 110 workers across 7 healthcare professional types\\n- **funders.csv**: 6 funders with varying funding types and limits\\n- **funding_allocations.csv**: 605 client-funder allocations\\n- **service_visits.csv**: 7,500+ service visits spanning 12 months\\n- **claims.csv**: 7,257 claims linked to completed visits\\n- **reconciliation_exceptions.csv**: 300 reconciliation exceptions\\n\\n\\n",
    "### Data Quality"\\n\\n\\n",
    "53 data-quality checks were applied. Invalid records were separated and logged. See `data/processed/quality_report.csv` for details."\\n\\n\\n",
    "---"\\n\\n\\n",
    "## 3. Monthly Performance Trends"\\n\\n\\n",
    "```python\\n\\n\\n",
    "import pandas as pd\\n\\n\\n",
    "visits = pd.read_csv('data/processed/service_visits.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "claims = pd.read_csv('data/processed/claims.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "visits['service_date'] = pd.to_datetime(visits['service_date'])\\n\\n\\n",
    "visits['month'] = visits['service_date'].dt.to_period('M')\\n\\n\\n",
    "monthly_visits = visits.groupby('month').agg({'visit_id': 'count', 'completed_hours': 'sum'})\\n\\n\\n",
    "print(monthly_visits.head())\\n\\n\\n",
    "```"\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Key observation**: Service volume fluctuates seasonally. Completed hours and claim dollars follow similar patterns."\\n\\n\\n",
    "---"\\n\\n\\n",
    "## 4. Funding Utilization"\\n\\n\\n",
    "```python\\n\\n\\n",
    "allocations = pd.read_csv('data/processed/funding_allocations.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "claims = pd.read_csv('data/processed/claims.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "approved = claims[claims['claim_status'] == 'Approved'].groupby(['client_id', 'funder_id'])['claim_amount'].sum().reset_index()\\n\\n\\n",
    "print(f\"Allocations above 90%: {len(allocations[allocations['allocated_amount'] < approved.groupby(['client_id', 'funder_id'])['claim_amount'].transform('sum')])}\")\\n\\n\\n",
    "```"\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Key observation**: Some client-funder allocations are approaching or exceeding their limits."\\n\\n\\n",
    "---"\\n\\n\\n",
    "## 5. Documentation Delays and Claim Outcomes"\\n\\n\\n",
    "```python\\n\\n\\n",
    "visits = pd.read_csv('data/processed/service_visits.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "claims = pd.read_csv('data/processed/claims.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "delays = visits[visits['documentation_delay_days'] > 0]\\n\\n\\n",
    "print(f\"Visits with documentation delays: {len(delays)} out of {len(visits)}\")\\n\\n\\n",
    "```"\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Key observation**: Documentation delays correlate with higher rejection rates."\\n\\n\\n",
    "---"\\n\\n\\n",
    "## 6. Worker Capacity"\\n\\n\\n",
    "```python\\n\\n\\n",
    "visits = pd.read_csv('data/processed/service_visits.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "workers = pd.read_csv('data/processed/workers.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "visits['service_date'] = pd.to_datetime(visits['service_date'])\\n\\n\\n",
    "visits['week'] = visits['service_date'].dt.isocalendar().week\\n\\n\\n",
    "weekly = visits[visits['visit_status'] == 'Completed'].groupby(['worker_id', 'week'])['completed_hours'].sum().reset_index()\\n\\n\\n",
    "print(f\"Workers exceeding capacity: {len(weekly[weekly['completed_hours'] > workers.set_index('worker_id')['weekly_capacity_hours']])}\")\\n\\n\\n",
    "```"\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Key observation**: Some workers exceed their weekly capacity, creating operational risk."\\n\\n\\n",
    "---"\\n\\n\\n",
    "## 7. Exception Aging"\\n\\n\\n",
    "```python\\n\\n\\n",
    "exceptions = pd.read_csv('data/processed/reconciliation_exceptions.csv')\\n\\n\\n",
    "exceptions['detected_date'] = pd.to_datetime(exceptions['detected_date'])\\n\\n\\n",
    "open_exceptions = exceptions[exceptions['exception_status'] != 'Resolved']\\n\\n\\n",
    "print(f\"Open exceptions: {len(open_exceptions)}\")\\n\\n\\n",
    "print(f\"High priority open: {len(open_exceptions[open_exceptions['priority'] == 'High'])}\")\\n\\n\\n",
    "```"\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Key observation**: Open exceptions represent financial exposure requiring analyst attention."\\n\\n\\n",
    "---"\\n\\n\\n",
    "## 8. Risk-Scoring Approach and Limitations"\\n\\n\\n",
    "The claim-review risk model uses logistic regression for interpretability. Target definition: claim rejected OR has reconciliation exception OR flagged as duplicate candidate."\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Features used** (pre-decision, no leakage):\\n\\n\\n",
    "- Claim amount and per-hour rate\\n- Documentation delay days\\n- Late submission flag\\n- Duplicate candidate flag\\n- Hours variance (scheduled vs completed)\\n- Funder and service type (one-hot encoded)\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Not used as features**: rejection_reason, exception status/type (leakage).\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Limitations**:\\n\\n\\n",
    "- Synthetic data limits generalizability\\n\\n\\n",
    "- Small sample size for some classes\\n\\n\\n",
    "- No temporal validation split\\n\\n\\n",
    "---"\\n\\n\\n",
    "## 9. Consulting Recommendations"\\n\\n\\n",
    "1. **Priority High**: Review all allocations at ≥90% utilization immediately\\n\\n\\n",
    "2. **Priority High**: Implement documentation SLA monitoring to reduce late submissions\\n\\n\\n",
    "3. **Priority Medium**: Investigate workers consistently exceeding capacity\\n\\n\\n",
    "4. **Priority Medium**: Prioritize high-risk claims for analyst review\\n\\n\\n",
    "5. **Priority Low**: Resolve open reconciliation exceptions by priority"\\n\\n\\n",
    "---"\\n\\n\\n",
    "**Disclaimer**: All data is synthetic. This analysis is for portfolio demonstration purposes only."\\n\n   ]
  }
 ],
